@startuml
title Hydrological Data To Flow Runtime Path
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 180
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

rectangle "External datasets\nrecharge, ETP, runoff,\nhydrography, oceanic" as Data
rectangle "Data managers\nLoadResult payloads" as Load

rectangle "Structure binders\nbind recharge / ETP /\nboundary payloads" as Binders
rectangle "forcing_bridge.resolve_forcing()\nspatial mode + time alignment\nunit normalization" as Bridge
rectangle "FlowRechargeConfig\nFlowEtpConfig\nboundary mappings" as FlowCfg
rectangle "Flow runtime" as Flow
rectangle "Solver adapters\nMODFLOW-NWT / MODFLOW 6 /\nBoussinesq" as Solvers

rectangle "Calibration / comparison\nrunoff remains observation-side\nand may be added to DRN/baseflow" as Eval

Data --> Load
Load --> Binders : recharge, ETP,\nstage-capable inputs
Binders --> Bridge : diffuse forcing path
Bridge --> FlowCfg : mm/day -> m/s\nor stage in m
FlowCfg --> Flow
Flow --> Solvers

Load --> Eval : runoff
Flow --> Eval : simulated heads,\ndrainage, baseflow

note bottom of Bridge
Diffuse forcing and boundary support
share one Flow contract, but they are not
the same physical category.
end note
@enduml
